From 4e66fe06106a410965178f25b548524a0d95541b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shorinkiwata <fcl709@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:12:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Use frame threading for H.264 also for low-latency
 callers.

With MF_LOW_LATENCY set, the H.264 decoder only enabled slice threading.
Slice threading parallelizes the slices of one picture, so a stream coded
with a single slice per picture, which is common, is decoded on one
thread whatever the thread count. 3840x2160 video at 60 frames per second
then decodes slower than real time, and a player that drops late frames
shows nothing.

Enable frame threading as well. It delays the first output by a few
frames, which callers already handle since the decoder returns
MF_E_TRANSFORM_NEED_MORE_INPUT until a frame is ready.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
index 03e51cc26c4..b0a648bb23d 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -950,9 +950,12 @@ NTSTATUS transform_create( void *arg )
             int thread_count = av_cpu_count();
 
             /* libavcodec defaults to one thread. Bound the worker count like
-             * winegstreamer, without adding frame latency to low-latency callers. */
+             * winegstreamer. Frame threading is used even for low-latency
+             * callers: slice threading does nothing for streams coded with one
+             * slice per picture, which leaves high resolution, high frame rate
+             * video decoding on a single core, slower than real time. */
             t->avctx->thread_count = max( 1, min( thread_count, sizeof(void *) == 4 ? 4 : 16 ) );
-            t->avctx->thread_type = params->low_latency ? FF_THREAD_SLICE : FF_THREAD_SLICE | FF_THREAD_FRAME;
+            t->avctx->thread_type = FF_THREAD_SLICE | FF_THREAD_FRAME;
         }
         else if (is_wmv_video_codec( codec_id ))
         {
